{
  "about": "EXPR-7 case item order: a case's items are when/then items, then at most one otherwise item, last. A case with no when/then item, written with only an otherwise item or with no item, fails validation at the case (at least one when/then item), and an otherwise item that another item follows fails at that item (otherwise only as the last item), each as invalid_field_type, at every expression site: a column derivation, a case nested in a then, a row template's derivation, an intermediate's derivation and an aggregate's derivation. A case of two otherwise items reports both findings, the case's first. The finding names the file the run loaded, as its source and entry. check and the build report the same complete rows. negative-case-otherwise-only states the first site's first issue, but its error.yaml leaves out the layer the finding names and that the issue is the only one; no benchmark pins the other sites. Moved from the case_item_order module of execution_aggregate_record_operations.rs at db988eb9c: each specification is the test's Fixture text, its header followed by the body each site wrote, written here as the spec document with the edits that make that body, and dm.csv and ex.csv are the files the test wrote. Each issue row is the test's finding(path, expected), compared at the five fields support::study::issue_row projects, in a complete list as the test compared it. The tests ran check and the build for the Python and the R host. The host is read only for a project's environment, functions or lock, and no case names a project, so each specification is one case, and case_api_contracts.rs makes the R calls. No engine output supplied these values.",
